      "datasource": {
        "type": "elasticsearch",
        "uid": "es-logs"
      },
      "description": "Where the errors actually are. Grouped by dataset, then by the two different ways a document says where it came from: agent-collected logs set host.name, while anything pushed to a UDP listener — the QNAP, every UniFi device — sets observer.name and no host.name at all. Both columns use a missing bucket, because a terms aggregation silently drops documents that lack the field, and grouping on host.name alone would leave every network device off the table rather than showing it with the column blank. Counts documents the ingest pipeline failed to parse as well as error-level logs: those carry no log.level, and a parse failure is an error worth seeing here.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 36,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 9
      },
